reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/CONCLUSIONS.md:19:Reconstruct identical saved candidate requests; interleave fresh no-score controls with true-score requests and a score-shuffled control, with fixed score representation and randomization, repeated draws, cache misses, and identical model, candidates and question content except score lines. Make each score's query origin explicit: multiple search queries may yield different scores. A shuffled control tests sensitivity to a number but needs care with singleton/equal-score cases and preserving query origin. A source-blind independent reader judges differing pairs and controls without seeing arm, score, or prior decision. Report wrong merges, missed repeats, incorrect revision classifications and group choices separately, all cases, with same-arm variability, cost and limitations; fixed-candidate comparisons do not prove forward-run performance. The fresh set has few or no revisions; use separately identified stored revision cases without presenting isolated pair results as product-path evidence. Freeze design, audit and preflight under repository rules before any paid send. A score can also encode context Jev did not directly receive (e.g. thesis wording or period), so improvement would not itself establish the mechanism.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:3:For example, the known X22 error grouped a report of **commercial deliveries** with an earlier report about **production status and a revenue-share forecast**. Both original readers called those different facts. A useful probe must establish whether giving Jev the real search score improves that decision without causing other wrong groupings—and must not describe a shuffled score as though it were the real similarity. [Source packet]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-packet-1.json:882), [reader verdicts]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-answer.json:14).
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:7:1. **The shuffled arm makes a factual claim that is deliberately false.** The proposed text calls the numbers “Retrieval cosine similarities (query-to-stored-text),” while the placebo permutes them between candidates. It also retains an “origin query.” A score transferred from candidate A to B is no longer B’s similarity; its claimed origin or top-ten retrieval status can conflict with the number. [Design]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:7). The whole request otherwise asks Jev to “Use only the supplied text” to classify repeat, revision, or different, using words, source, speaker and time. The new numbers can encode thesis and period information Jev does not see, and can distract from that factual comparison. [Comparison request]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:40), [criteria]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:54), [contract]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:155).
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:17:   **Recommendation:** have independent readers classify the incoming statement against the relevant candidate set and sources without scores, rank, arm or model answer; then compare those classifications with each arm’s complete outcome, including the selected group and revisions. Record unresolved cases and actual review coverage. If only a subset is reviewed, report observed errors in that subset rather than accuracy or missed-repeat totals for all ten.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:19:4. **The decision and stopping rule are not yet executable.** The design says to “predeclare a compact decision before send,” but also leaves “material” harm and “balancing demonstrated gain” undefined. It predicts a better X22 result and no worsening of accepted repeats, yet permits balancing harm against gain. [Design]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:50). Three stochastic draws do not have a natural one-to-one pairing across arms; a difference in individual draws alone does not establish a score effect.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:27:The design correctly limits its claims: the earlier **141/143** result measures search among available repeat pairs, while **1/57** is a wrong-merge count; neither is Jev repeat recall. The prior report also says one 11-member story accounts for 55 pairs and revisions were barely exercised. [Fresh log]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1614), [limitations]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1668). Holding candidates fixed is suitable for this small diagnostic, but cannot show improved retrieval or forward-path performance.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:15:Two independent readers label pairs **repeat, revision, different-party forecast of the same quantity, or different**. The third label is an analysis subtype of *different*, not a fourth Jev outcome. Readers can mark insufficient information rather than guess. Resolve disagreements against the source and record both original labels and the reason. Readers must see both complete summaries, all source passages and enough surrounding article context, reporting source, original claimant, publication and stated dates, tier, period, figures and qualifications, plus associated thesis descriptions. Hide search ranks and Jev answers.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:17:Estimate missed positive pairs by checking how many repeats and revisions in the exhaustive sampled articles were absent from the pooled generator. Report the sampling method, raw counts, uncertainty and an appropriately weighted estimate; also report misses by cross-thesis and relationship type. If the sample finds too few positives to estimate this usefully, expand it before claiming recall. An exhaustive sample estimates missed pairs; it does not prove the remaining reference is complete.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:39:**Open for Alex:** if one incoming item is labelled repeat of one candidate and revision of another, or repeats of several candidates, what should be saved? Do not invent a winner or simulate a definitive dossier outcome until that is decided. The [PRD](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:143>) leaves conflicting and uncertain candidates open.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:41:[D168](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2338>) permits cross-thesis repeats but bounded replacement to the same thesis in the older path; its revision definition is useful prior evidence, not automatic approval of cross-thesis revision behavior. [D202](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2594>) keeps both sides of a revision. [D204](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2610>) preserved both repeat texts after 8 of 40 sampled prior repeats lost different or richer content. Alex’s later clean-design choice is to reuse a repeat record and add the source and missing link ([PRD §6](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:161>)); the earlier loss remains a risk to measure, not a reason to silently reverse that choice.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:47:- **Retrieval:** recall at 10 for all labelled earlier repeat and revision pairs, separately by type and cross-thesis status. Also report the share of incoming associations for which at least one acceptable prior target is found. Show counts and uncertainty, including estimated generator misses.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:48:- **Comparison:** confusion matrix on independently sampled pairs and on retrieved candidates; report repeat and revision recall separately, plus revision incorrectly labelled repeat.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:51:- **Three dossiers:** report records per thesis before and after deduplication, sources and links retained, revisions visible, and manually inspect whether meaningful qualifications disappear. Label this a simulation until conflict handling is decided.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/a-codex.md:60:4. **Cents:** send the fixed Jev requests on labelled pairs, including hard negatives and revisions, then on retrieved candidates. If it repeatedly turns changed or richer statements into repeats, the proposed saving behavior is unsafe at the measured rate.
