reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/RESULTS.md:7:The seventh case's first dispatch (`18:e2`, treatment draw 1) failed with `ConnectionResetError` after 36 successful answers. Whether that request reached the service is unknown. Per the predeclared single-attempt stop rule it was not retried; 29 further planned calls were not sent. Six cases have all six answers; five cases have no complete paired result. In particular the known wrong merge (`22:ev-11`) and revision-bearing example (`19:ev-guidance-70`) were not reached. Six completed cases carry 46 candidate comparisons; control and treatment each have three decisions per candidate. Logged successful input tokens 136,590, logged cost $0.005742; the ambiguous request's actual billing is unknown.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/RESULTS.md:11:Every one of the 46 candidate relation choices was identical in all six draws. The resulting groups and revision links were also identical in all six: 3:e1 repeat of 1:e3; 5:e1 new; 9:e1 new; 9:e6 repeat of 7:E1; 13:e11 repeat of 6:e1; 14:e3 repeat of 7:E4. No revision links occurred. For 5 of the 46 candidate comparisons, the mean reported same-statement probability differed across the arms; one example was 9:e6 against 7:E1, control 0.77/0.74/0.79, treatment 0.84/0.84/0.86. Probabilities do not establish accuracy or explain a cause.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/RESULTS.md:13:Two independent blind readers each read source materials and all 46 candidates for these cases, and agreed: 3 same, 42 different, 1 overlap. In particular 13:e11 groups a three-cloud growth record into an AWS-only record; both blind readers call it an overlap. Do not count that as unambiguously right or wrong. The other three repeat targets were both called same, and both new cases had no candidates called same or revision. Later details remain preserved as member text; the score does not fix the overlap.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/RESULTS.md:17:No visible decision benefit or harm in the six completed selected cases. This is not evidence of equivalence or a measured precision/recall change. The wrong-merge case central to the prediction and the revision-bearing case were not run. The score input also adds query-type metadata and can encode thesis/period content missing from the comparator; an effect could not be attributed to numerical similarity alone. Complete result and two source-backed reviews do not exist for the intended 11 cases. Stop and report the interruption, no automatic resumption or replacement of the ambiguous call. The independent Codex partial review is `partial-review.out`; independent Claude follow-up is `partial-claude.jsonl`. No adoption or product change is justified by these results.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/c-codex.md:3:**(a) Re-label, but keep two questions separate.** First ask whether the records contain the same statement, a revision, or different statements. Then, independently, ask what material information the later record adds and whether the proposed source-only merge would preserve it. A record can repeat one statement *and* contain a separate new fact. Forcing that into one of five exclusive labels would conceal the overlap.
clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/council/c-codex.md:14:Finally, six generator misses among 40 labelled sample positives and the summary-first scan limit completeness. Report uncertainty and examine missed revisions and cross-thesis cases separately. Do not send Jev comparisons until the corrected reference and scoring unit are settled.
